# Kursor by Intech — environment configuration reference.
#
# The panel itself only reads these three (internal/config/config.go);
# everything else here documents ports/services Kursor's own modules
# manage on the host once you turn them on from the UI — see PORTS.md
# for the full picture (what each port is, and when you actually need
# it open).
#
# install.sh writes KURSOR_ADDR/KURSOR_DATA_DIR/KURSOR_WWW_ROOT straight
# into the systemd unit as Environment= lines — this file is a reference
# for manual/Docker-less runs (`env $(cat configs/kursor.env | xargs) kursord`),
# not something the binary loads automatically.

# --- read directly by kursord ---------------------------------------------
KURSOR_ADDR=:8888
KURSOR_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/kursor
KURSOR_WWW_ROOT=/var/www/kursor

# --- read by scripts/install.sh only (picks the panel's listen port) ------
KURSOR_PORT=8888
